1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,989
This is our capstone:

2
00:00:02,039 --> 00:00:07,576
an intelligent dental assisting system that
reads a panoramic X-ray, tooth by tooth.

3
00:00:08,976 --> 00:00:14,278
A panoramic radiograph, or OPG,
shows every tooth in one image.

4
00:00:14,328 --> 00:00:16,941
A dentist reads it tooth by tooth.

5
00:00:16,991 --> 00:00:18,376
We automate that reading:

6
00:00:18,426 --> 00:00:23,514
find each tooth, number it in FDI
notation, and report its findings.

7
00:00:24,914 --> 00:00:29,081
Our six-stage pipeline takes one radiograph
and returns a per-tooth report and an

8
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:34,190
annotated overlay, in about one point seven
seconds on CPU alone, with ninety-five

9
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:38,060
million parameters, inside
a Streamlit and Docker demo.

10
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:41,182
It is built on public data:

11
00:00:41,232 --> 00:00:46,106
the Tufts database of a thousand radiographs,
the DENTEX challenge set, and the

12
00:00:46,156 --> 00:00:48,306
CariesXrays benchmark.

13
00:00:48,356 --> 00:00:53,230
Four Ningxia hospitals are held out as
external test data, never trained on, and

14
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:57,742
UFBA-425 is unseen by our
detector and numbering head.

15
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:01,531
One question shaped the project.

16
00:01:01,581 --> 00:01:06,009
Caries concentrates in the molars, so a
rule that ignores the image, and always

17
00:01:06,059 --> 00:01:11,205
names the same eight molars, already scores
well on the usual tooth-level metric.

18
00:01:11,255 --> 00:01:15,504
Every result here is measured
against that image-blind constant.

19
00:01:16,904 --> 00:01:21,869
Now, the architecture, following one
real radiograph through every stage.

20
00:01:21,919 --> 00:01:26,641
It is one of the one hundred and sixty-four
DENTEX evaluation images, about three

21
00:01:26,691 --> 00:01:29,306
thousand by fifteen hundred pixels.

22
00:01:30,706 --> 00:01:31,656
Stage one:

23
00:01:31,652 --> 00:01:33,171
tooth detection.

24
00:01:33,221 --> 00:01:37,802
A YOLO eleven large detector, trained on
three corpora, reads the image rotated

25
00:01:37,852 --> 00:01:40,291
ninety degrees and maps its boxes back:

26
00:01:40,341 --> 00:01:44,836
thirty-two teeth, every one above
zero point seven nine confidence.

27
00:01:46,236 --> 00:01:47,186
Stage two:

28
00:01:47,149 --> 00:01:48,451
numbering.

29
00:01:48,501 --> 00:01:52,766
Each tooth is cropped with a margin, and
passed with its position to a ResNet-18

30
00:01:52,816 --> 00:01:55,451
head that predicts its FDI code.

31
00:01:55,501 --> 00:01:57,919
A one-to-one assignment forbids duplicates:

32
00:01:57,969 --> 00:02:01,110
thirty-two teeth, thirty-two distinct codes.

33
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:03,503
Stage three:

34
00:02:03,553 --> 00:02:04,790
caries.

35
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:09,312
A second YOLO detector finds the lesions
themselves, across the whole image:

36
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:11,421
nine lesion boxes.

37
00:02:11,471 --> 00:02:16,112
Each is assigned to the tooth it
overlaps most, so nine teeth are flagged.

38
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:22,162
A severity head grades each flagged
tooth as caries or deep caries.

39
00:02:22,212 --> 00:02:25,412
Teeth twenty-one and
forty-six are graded deep.

40
00:02:25,462 --> 00:02:29,098
This head is validated, but
it has never been tested.

41
00:02:30,498 --> 00:02:33,398
Stage four is an abnormality flag.

42
00:02:33,448 --> 00:02:38,496
A ResNet-18 reads a taller crop around each
tooth and flags closeness to an expert-marked

43
00:02:38,546 --> 00:02:39,496
abnormality:

44
00:02:39,502 --> 00:02:43,126
here, teeth eleven,
thirty-seven and forty-eight.

45
00:02:43,176 --> 00:02:47,916
It is not a periodontal diagnosis,
and its severity grade is withheld.

46
00:02:49,316 --> 00:02:54,255
Stages five and six fuse it all into one
record per tooth, in report schema one

47
00:02:54,305 --> 00:02:58,249
point five, stamped with the
hash of every model that ran.

48
00:02:58,299 --> 00:03:02,054
The overlay shows findings in
orange, and the rest in blue.

49
00:03:03,454 --> 00:03:08,078
Against the dentists' annotations, seven
of the nine caries flags land on annotated

50
00:03:08,128 --> 00:03:11,626
carious teeth, and four
annotated teeth are missed.

51
00:03:11,676 --> 00:03:14,550
That is one image, for illustration.

52
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,056
The measured numbers come next.

53
00:03:18,456 --> 00:03:19,406
Part three:

54
00:03:19,369 --> 00:03:21,639
results across the timeline.

55
00:03:21,689 --> 00:03:27,769
In August, the pipeline ran end to end, and
was validated on four external hospitals.

56
00:03:27,819 --> 00:03:29,943
Then came the uncomfortable finding:

57
00:03:29,993 --> 00:03:33,084
the image-blind constant tied or beat us.

58
00:03:33,134 --> 00:03:37,595
On the fourth of September, a lesion
detector became the first method to beat it,

59
00:03:37,645 --> 00:03:39,762
on two of three cohorts.

60
00:03:41,162 --> 00:03:44,866
On the tenth of October, a
review audited every number.

61
00:03:44,916 --> 00:03:48,845
It found that the bone-loss score of zero
point nine two came from a split that

62
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:54,116
shared radiographs with training, and that
its label was not periodontal bone loss.

63
00:03:58,162 --> 00:04:00,399
First, the front end.

64
00:04:00,449 --> 00:04:04,138
A multi-corpus tooth detector
replaced the old one.

65
00:04:04,188 --> 00:04:09,519
On DENTEX, tooth recall rose from seventy-one
to over ninety-nine percent, and numbering

66
00:04:09,569 --> 00:04:13,345
from fifty-eight to ninety-three,
in-domain for the new detector.

67
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:18,671
On the unseen UFBA-425 set, numbering rose
from twenty-one to forty-four and a half

68
00:04:18,721 --> 00:04:19,964
percent.

69
00:04:20,014 --> 00:04:20,964
The cost:

70
00:04:20,797 --> 00:04:25,900
Tufts box accuracy fell from zero point
seven two to zero point five nine.

71
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:32,478
For caries, the pipeline's F1 rose from
zero point three eight to zero point five,

72
00:04:32,528 --> 00:04:35,120
against zero point three
two for the constant:

73
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:39,396
a lead of nearly eighteen points,
with its interval clear of zero.

74
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:44,113
Across the four Ningxia hospitals, lesion
agreement reached sixty-eight percent,

75
00:04:44,163 --> 00:04:46,662
nine points above the constant.

76
00:04:48,062 --> 00:04:52,625
Stage four moved the other way,
because its old figure was inflated.

77
00:04:52,675 --> 00:04:57,679
On unseen radiographs, the original model
found seven point six percent of its label,

78
00:04:57,729 --> 00:04:59,408
not eighty-three.

79
00:04:59,458 --> 00:05:03,864
Retrained with a radiograph-level split,
it reaches twenty-seven and a half percent

80
00:05:03,914 --> 00:05:08,549
sensitivity at ninety-six percent specificity,
and eleven to twenty-seven percent

81
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,505
across three seeds.

82
00:05:10,555 --> 00:05:13,799
The severity head had
learned image contrast.

83
00:05:13,849 --> 00:05:19,496
Retrained on the true bands, it lost to a
position prior, so its grade stays withheld.

84
00:05:20,896 --> 00:05:24,176
Behind every number is a saved artefact.

85
00:05:24,226 --> 00:05:27,829
Automatically checked claims in the paper
went from one hundred twenty-seven to

86
00:05:27,879 --> 00:05:32,676
two hundred six, tests from one seventy-four
to one ninety-seven, and every default

87
00:05:32,726 --> 00:05:34,570
model is hash-pinned.

88
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:40,235
So the review lowered the numbers that were
inflated, raised the ones a better front

89
00:05:40,285 --> 00:05:44,340
end earned, and named every stage
for what it really measures.

90
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:46,690
Next:

91
00:05:46,425 --> 00:05:51,299
a six-page conference paper, built from
these verified numbers, and a venue decision

92
00:05:51,349 --> 00:05:52,847
with our mentor.

93
00:05:52,897 --> 00:05:54,230
Thank you.
